course: dictionary
lesson: 5763
title: A lullaby is a gentle song
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A lullaby is a soft, gentle song that helps a baby or small child fall asleep. People have sung lullabies for hundreds of years, and every country has its own. The song you hear just before bed, when you are sleepy, is a lullaby.
explain: Lullabies are slow and rocking, like a boat on calm water. The tune goes up and down gently, so the music calms the listener. Mums, dads, grans and carers often hum a lullaby, even when they do not sing the words.
explain: The word can also mean any soft, calming sound. «The lullaby of the waves» means the gentle, steady sound of the sea that makes you feel sleepy. The waves are not singing, but their sound rocks you like a lullaby.
explain: Writers sometimes twist a lullaby on purpose. In Alice in Wonderland, «the Duchess sings the baby a horrible lullaby». Readers notice because a real lullaby is gentle, so the word horrible is a clue that this song is shocking and rude, not calm.
fact: A lullaby is a soft, gentle song sung to help a baby or small child fall asleep.
fact: «Hush, Little Baby», «Rock-a-bye Baby» and «Twinkle, Twinkle, Little Star» are famous lullabies.
fact: Brahms wrote a famous lullaby, and every culture has its own lullabies.
fact: Lullabies often have slow, rocking rhythms.
fact: «Sing a lullaby» and «hum a lullaby» are common phrases.
exercise: What is a lullaby? | A shout to wake everyone up | A loud march for a parade | *A soft, gentle song to help a small child fall asleep | A fast, bouncy dance
exercise: «The lullaby of the waves» means what? | A song sung by fishermen at sea | *A soft, calming, rocking sound | A loud crash that wakes people up | A sharp, cold wind
exercise: «The Duchess sings the baby a horrible lullaby.» Why is the word horrible a clue? | It shows the baby is happy and fast asleep | It shows the song is very quiet | *It shows the song is not gentle, so the author is twisting a lullaby | Horrible means the same as gentle
test: Which phrase means singing softly to help a baby sleep? | Shout a warning | Count the stairs | *Sing a lullaby | Paint a picture
test: Which of these is a famous lullaby? | March to the Drum | Loud Thunder Song | *Rock-a-bye Baby | Ring Around the Park
exam: Why would a writer call a song a horrible lullaby? | To show the song is perfect for bedtime | To show it is a famous Scottish song | To show the baby is wide awake and happy | *To show a shocking twist on a gentle song, not a calm one
